# Two arms of arity one, both matching this package's own err, and only one of
# them is reported.
#
# `recover` is fed by the written call site below. `quiet` is never called, so
# nothing reaches its parameter and it stays silent. The two differ only in
# their NAME: provenance keys its fixpoint on (name, arity), and if that key
# ever stops distinguishing them — a collapsed group, a hash that ignores the
# name — `quiet` inherits what `recover` was fed and is reported for a rescue it
# never made.
#
# This used to lean on the pub self-seed, which retired with gavel 24. A call
# site proves the same thing and proves it from the program rather than from an
# assumption about callers nobody can see.
type woe
  at

fn boom _
  err (woe 5)

fn recover (err w:woe)
  w.at

fn quiet (err w:woe)
  w.at

pub fn asked _
  recover (boom 0)
